Build a four-panel patchwork figure to inspect potential contamination
from negative-control samples (extraction blanks, PCR blanks, etc.).

Panels:
\itemize{
\item \strong{A} boxplots of total reads and taxa richness per sample, split by
negative-control status.
\item \strong{B} dumbbell of the top contaminant taxa (mean relative abundance in NC
vs real samples), with mean read counts annotated above each point.
\item \strong{C} heatmap of the taxa detected in any negative control across all
samples; absences are drawn in white, columns are faceted by NC status.
\item \strong{D} PCoA ordination (Bray-Curtis by default) with samples coloured by NC
status.
}

The patchwork subtitle reports the number of real and negative-control
samples. To \emph{flag} or \emph{classify} negative-control taxa programmatically, see
\code{tidypq::identify_contam_negcontrol_pq()}; this function is the visual
companion.
